§ `ss 5(1), 13 and 14 -- lawful and unlawful non-citizens`

-- lawful: Priya on her student visa, 2019; Priya a citizen in 2030. unlawful: the Chennai engineer in Perth with no visa; still in Chennai.
#ASSERT `is a lawful non-citizen` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `is a lawful non-citizen` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `is an unlawful non-citizen` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `is an unlawful non-citizen` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `ss 29 and 30 -- permanent and temporary`

-- 801 (remain indefinitely); 820 (until a decision on the 801 -- an event; the term is in the Regulations, ASSUMED).
#ASSERT `is a permanent visa` `indefinitely`
#ASSERT NOT `is a permanent visa` `until a specified event happens`

#ASSERT `is a temporary visa` `until a specified event happens`

§ `ss 5F and 5CB -- what the relationship must show`

#ASSERT `are spouses under s 5F` `Daniel and Priya, January 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `are spouses under s 5F` `a married couple separated for good`
#ASSERT NOT `are spouses under s 5F` `a marriage of convenience`
#ASSERT NOT `are spouses under s 5F` `a couple whose marriage is invalid but who live together`

#ASSERT NOT `are de facto partners under s 5CB` `a married couple separated for good`
#ASSERT `are de facto partners under s 5CB` `an unmarried couple living together`
#ASSERT `are de facto partners under s 5CB` `an unmarried couple apart for a year's secondment`
#ASSERT `are de facto partners under s 5CB` `a couple whose marriage is invalid but who live together`
#ASSERT NOT `are de facto partners under s 5CB` `half-siblings living together`

§ `s 65 -- decision on the application`

-- Priya's 820, January 2025, as the facts record it granted; the relationship found not genuine; the charge unpaid; processing suspended.
#ASSERT `the s 65 decision` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `grant the visa`
#ASSERT `the s 65 decision` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `refuse to grant the visa`
#ASSERT `the s 65 decision` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `refuse to grant the visa`
#ASSERT `the s 65 decision` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no decision under s 65 yet`

